# {{appNameBase}} SDK - AI Agent Reference

## Installation

Add to your `Gemfile`:

```ruby
gem '{{gemName}}'
```

Then run:

```bash
bundle install
```

## Quick Start

```ruby
require '{{gemName}}'

client = {{moduleName}}::{{clientClassName}}.with_token('https://api.example.com', 'your-token')
```

## Authentication

All authentication is handled via `Authenticator` implementations passed to the client constructor.

### Bearer Token

```ruby
authenticator = {{moduleName}}::Auth::BearerAuthenticator.new('https://api.example.com', 'your-token')
client = {{moduleName}}::{{clientClassName}}.new(authenticator)
```

{{#hasClientSchemes}}
### Credentials per security scheme

`{{clientClassName}}.new` takes one optional credential for each security scheme of the API, named after the scheme: {{#clientSchemes}}`{{argName}}:`{{^-last}}, {{/-last}}{{/clientSchemes}}. Each operation uses the credential of the first scheme in its own security requirement that you configured; there is no per-call override. An optional `authenticator` (the first argument) serves any operation no scheme credential matches, and an operation that declares no security sends no credential of its own. The client is refused, with an `ArgumentError`, when it gets no credential at all.

```ruby
# credential is the Auth::Authenticator you built for that scheme
client = {{moduleName}}::{{clientClassName}}.new(nil, nil, {{#clientSchemes}}{{#-first}}{{argName}}: credential{{/-first}}{{/clientSchemes}})
```

{{/hasClientSchemes}}
### Credentials from the environment

A credential you leave out is read, once, when the authenticator is built, from the environment variable of its security scheme; an empty variable counts as unset. The value you pass wins, and a Bearer token falls back to `token_provider:` (called for every request) when neither is set. A credential still missing raises `ArgumentError` before the client is built.
{{#hasSecuritySchemeEnvVars}}

| Security scheme | Credential | Environment variable |
|---|---|---|
{{#securitySchemeEnvVars}}
| `{{schemeId}}` | `{{fieldSnake}}` | `{{envName}}` |
{{/securitySchemeEnvVars}}
{{/hasSecuritySchemeEnvVars}}

